/-
Route 7.2 (c): the integer ring of an actual p-adic local field is monogenic over Z_p.

Setting.  p is prime and L is a finite extension of Q_p in the accepted local-field
interface: [NormedField L] [CharZero L] [CompleteSpace L] [IsUltrametricDist L]
[ProperSpace L] [NormedAlgebra Q_p L] [FiniteDimensional Q_p L].  Write O = Integers L
for the norm-integer ring (the valuation ring of L).

The main theorem of this file,

  nonempty_monogenicIntegers : Nonempty (MonogenicIntegers (p := p) (L := L)),

closes the residual gap recorded in Mzk1G1UniversalMonogenicExistenceActual: some single
element of O generates O over Z_p.  By exists_monogenicIntegers_of_residue_generator it
suffices to find x : O whose class generates the finite residue ring O/pO over F_p.

The construction is the classical Frobenius (freshman's dream) trick, carried out in
the quotient ring R = O / pO:

* pi is a uniformizer of the discrete valuation ring O and e >= 1 satisfies pi ^ e = p;
* beta lifts a primitive element of the residue field k = O/m over F_p, and
  Q = |k| = p ^ f, so beta ^ Q - beta lies in the maximal ideal m = (pi);
* with b, x the classes of beta, pi in R, the element B = b ^ (Q ^ e) satisfies B ^ Q = B
  (freshman's dream: B ^ Q - B = (b ^ Q - b) ^ (Q ^ e) = 0 because Q ^ e >= e and x ^ e = 0);
* for gamma = B + x one has gamma ^ (Q ^ e) = B ^ (Q ^ e) + x ^ (Q ^ e) = B, so both B and
  x = gamma - B lie in the Z_p-subalgebra generated by gamma;
* every element of R is congruent to a Z_p-polynomial in B modulo x (the residue field is
  generated by beta over F_p, and B is congruent to beta modulo x), so the nilpotence of x
  lets one iterate until R is exhausted.

Consequently every class in R is a Z_p-polynomial in the class of gamma = beta ^ (Q ^ e) + pi,
and the donor consumer exists_monogenicIntegers_of_residue_generator supplies the
monogenic presentation.
-/
import tmp.sheaf.xif.paper.Mzk1G1UniversalMonogenicExistenceActual
